  "details": "<p>The Barrington Atlas Directory notes: source of R. Cydara (Arevi-\u0101r) SRI</p>",
  "review_state": "published",
  "type": "FeatureCollection",
  "description": "Pliny the Elder describes the \"Megisba Stagnum\" as an inland marsh or lake of Sri Lanka that has a circumference of 375 Roman miles. He says that from this wetland once flowed two rivers: one called Palaesimundus and the other called Cydara.",
